From: Stained Glass OS contributors
Subject: shell32: an NSIS installer's elevated copy installs

NSIS's UAC plugin -- Firefox's installer and many others -- starts itself as
an administrator with /UAC:<window>, and the elevated copy calls back to that
window to do its work. An elevated program here runs on a display and desktop
of its own, the window is out of its reach, and the copy gave up at once:
"The installer finished, but Mozilla Firefox did not register". (Before
0448 the caller stopped waiting at once, the copy found no caller, and
installed by itself -- which it now does again: SgElevate leaves the /UAC:
switch out.)

Gate: test/elevreq-gate.sh (make test-elevreq).
---
--- a/dlls/shell32/shlexec.c
+++ b/dlls/shell32/shlexec.c
@@ -360,7 +360,7 @@
     LONG (WINAPI *spawnvp)( char * const argv[], int wait );
     char broker[MAX_PATH * 3] = "/usr/libexec/stained-glass/sg-elevate", **argv;
     WCHAR **args, value[MAX_PATH];
-    int count = 0, i, len;
+    int count = 0, i, len, n;
     WCHAR ** (WINAPI *to_argv)( const WCHAR *, int * );
     LONG ret;
 
@@ -372,11 +372,18 @@
     if (!(argv = calloc( count + 3, sizeof(*argv) ))) ExitProcess( 2 );
     argv[0] = broker;
     argv[1] = (char *)"--wine";
-    for (i = 0; i < count; i++)
+    for (i = 0, n = 2; i < count; i++)
     {
+        /* NSIS's UAC plugin (Firefox's installer, many others) starts itself
+         * elevated with /UAC:<window> and has the elevated copy call back to
+         * that window. An elevated program here is on a display and desktop
+         * of its own, where the window is out of reach, and the copy gave up
+         * and installed nothing. Without the switch the elevated copy installs
+         * by itself, as the plugin does when its caller is gone. */
+        if (!wcsnicmp( args[i], L"/UAC:", 5 )) continue;
         len = WideCharToMultiByte( CP_UNIXCP, 0, args[i], -1, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL );
-        if (!(argv[i + 2] = malloc( len ))) ExitProcess( 2 );
-        WideCharToMultiByte( CP_UNIXCP, 0, args[i], -1, argv[i + 2], len, NULL, NULL );
+        if (!(argv[n] = malloc( len ))) ExitProcess( 2 );
+        WideCharToMultiByte( CP_UNIXCP, 0, args[i], -1, argv[n++], len, NULL, NULL );
     }
     TRACE( "%s --wine with %d arguments\n", debugstr_a(broker), count );
     ret = spawnvp( argv, TRUE );
